                  <provenance type="#m"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_456">Ramsey,
                        Huntingdonshire. Benedictine Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin and St Benedict</orgName><p>At fol. 51v, 'Disce mori Dodisthorp' (s. xv); compare the 'quod
                        Dodisthorp' in a less careful hand in Bodley 851, and for the opening words,
                        compare Wisbech, Museum 5. Dodisthorp = Dogsthorp, near Peterborough but
                        this volume cannot come from Peterborough as a scribble on fol. 69v shows
                        that it comes from a Benedictine house dedicated to St Mary and St
                        [blank].</p></provenance>
